---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// Keep this page honest and fresh — update it when the facts change
const lastUpdated = 'August 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title="Now — Mihnea Catana" description="What Mihnea is working on, learning, and reading right now.">
  <section class="section container">
    <p class="label fade-up">Last updated — {lastUpdated}</p>
    <h1 class="h-display h2 reveal page-title">
      <span class="reveal-inner">What I'm doing <em class="accent-word">now.</em></span>
    </h1>

    <div class="prose prose--drop fade-up" style="--d: 1">
      <p>
        This is a <a href="https://nownownow.com/">/now page</a>: a snapshot of what I'm up to, updated whenever
        it changes enough to be worth reading.
      </p>

      <h2>Building</h2>
      <p>
        At Lenovo I'm deep in AI adoption — extending Atlassian tooling with AI skills, agents, hooks and MCP
        servers, and pushing that tooling out to teams across the department. On my own time, I'm growing the
        AI Agent Avatar Registry: a live registry where AI agents onboard themselves and show up as pixel
        avatars on a real-time feed.
      </p>

      <h2>Learning</h2>
      <p>
        Everything agentic: MCP server design, how multiple agents behave when they share a system, and where
        local models like Ollama can replace cloud calls without anyone noticing the difference.
      </p>

      <h2>Teaching</h2>
      <p>
        Frontend sessions for Lenovo's Summer School, mentoring, and interviewing — teaching is the fastest
        way to find the gaps in my own understanding.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-title {
    margin-top: 1.4rem;
    margin-bottom: clamp(2.2rem, 6vh, 3.5rem);
  }
</style>
